        "abstract": "The paper mill in North Carolina operates four paper machines and has been producing paper for over a century. Six, in-house, turbine-generators provide a share of the electrical power to the four paper machines while also providing steam for the paper-making process. A power system study completed in 2015 identified several areas where improvements could be made in the reliability and safety of the mill auxiliary power system [1]. This paper covers the work necessary to update the mill power system study for the latest round of improvements and includes a few lessons learned from the field application side.",
