        "abstract": "With full-voltage starts on induction motors, locked rotor current and asymmetric inrush current occur. Using reduced-voltage soft starters (RVSS) the AC phase current is ramped and limited to a value less than the locked rotor value. This extends the start time. In this paper, the torque per Ampere versus speed are shown from the two starting approaches. The temperature of the stator winding and results from a vibration sensor are illustrated. In addition the enhanced soft stopping approaches using an RVSS are compared to a coast stop. Lastly, results from lightly loaded forced RVSS brake stops using DC and an AC approach are shown.",
