                "firstName": "Dante E.",
                "lastName": "Barragan"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The term Social Media conjures up a host of reactions as diverse as the readers of this article. To some individuals, dedicating time to social media is simply an opportunity to unwind in front of a computer or cellphone screen. To industry employers, social media might be considered an opportunity for outreach/advertising to a target group of customers as a part of a new initiative to launch a new company product or service. Conversely, social media could be perceived as a potential disruption in employee productivity, allowing workers to easily be distracted from commitment to their daily work. Or even worse, perhaps it could pose a threat to the business, where valued employees might easily identify opportunities to work for another company.The purpose of this article is to share the experiences of one industry focused technical committee of the world’s largest technical organization, the Institute of Electrical & Electronic Engineers (IEEE), and their quest to leverage social media to increase awareness and inspire interest by industry stakeholders to attend the committee’s annual technical conference. The paper will identify the stated objective of a committee Ad Hoc group in developing a social media web portal, explore advantages and disadvantages of various social media platforms and share findings and results from the outreach effort.",
